"Queue removed; rounds + pinned bar landed (commit 81a92a6, user-directed): (1) actions authored as ROUNDS -- ActionRoundAuthor { effects } lists everything resolving in ONE system tick; action system applies all effects of the current round per tick; finish = empty next round. ActionStep table unchanged (rows may share sequence_index). Codegen note: Vec<Vec<ActionEffect>> hit a TS-codegen TDZ bug (nested array of a later-declared enum is not getter-wrapped) -- the named round struct sidesteps it. (2) Most battle actions single-round (boppity_bop = two attacks in one round = the grouped-effects showcase); move keeps a 3-round wind-up, slime_spray a 1-round telegraph. (3) Queue panel deleted; the space is the pinned-actions bar: PinnedActionsComponent (ordered action_ids) replaces ActionHotkeysComponent; bar position auto-assigns numeric hotkeys 1..9,0; pinned buttons bind the FOCUS (no explicit target) so lone-hostile auto-focus + a digit = a complete battle turn. Entity panels ceded their numeric hotkeys to the bar. NEW_PLAYER_BLOB pins boppity_bop/quick_move/divine_heal. (4) Old Target* stubs and the dead useSetActionHotkey stub actually deleted (rm now permitted). Server queued_action_state machinery retained (act -> queued -> shift) -- only the UI queue display died. Full gate green (cargo, clippy, check, 103 unit, e2e 0-6 incl. single-round combat)."